1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,066
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:02,829 --> 00:00:06,311
Lesson 3: Worlds Weather and Climate.

3
00:00:08,371 --> 00:00:09,602
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:11,602 --> 00:00:13,001
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:13,601 --> 00:00:14,902
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:15,963 --> 00:00:18,845
Explain the difference between weather and climate.

7
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:23,108
Identify and describe the factors affecting climate.

8
00:00:23,869 --> 00:00:26,431
Understand the different types of climate found

9
00:00:26,511 --> 00:00:27,032
in the world.

10
00:00:27,872 --> 00:00:30,334
Recognize the climatic zones of the Earth.

11
00:00:31,195 --> 00:00:33,977
Explain how climate affects human life and

12
00:00:34,057 --> 00:00:34,777
the environment.

13
00:00:36,357 --> 00:00:36,984
Start-Up.

14
00:00:38,984 --> 00:00:40,125
Look outside the window!

15
00:00:40,826 --> 00:00:41,446
Is it sunny,

16
00:00:41,966 --> 00:00:43,288
cloudy, or rainy?

17
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:45,930
Have you ever noticed how the weather

18
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:47,271
changes throughout the day?

19
00:00:48,091 --> 00:00:49,933
Some places are always warm,

20
00:00:50,393 --> 00:00:51,674
while others are cold.

21
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:53,356
Why does this happen?

22
00:00:54,156 --> 00:00:54,957
In this chapter,

23
00:00:55,477 --> 00:00:57,999
we will explore the differences between weather

24
00:00:58,199 --> 00:01:01,022
and climate and understand the factors that

25
00:01:01,162 --> 00:01:01,862
influence them.

26
00:01:03,482 --> 00:01:03,890
Weather.

27
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:08,344
Weather is the condition of the atmosphere

28
00:01:08,605 --> 00:01:10,406
at a particular place and time.

29
00:01:11,307 --> 00:01:12,588
It includes temperature,

30
00:01:13,088 --> 00:01:15,631
wind, rainfall, humidity,

31
00:01:16,011 --> 00:01:16,832
and cloud cover.

32
00:01:17,692 --> 00:01:19,774
Weather can change from hour to hour

33
00:01:20,135 --> 00:01:20,815
or day to day.

34
00:01:21,636 --> 00:01:23,497
For example, one morning,

35
00:01:23,778 --> 00:01:25,940
it may be sunny and by afternoon

36
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:26,900
it could rain.

37
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,053
Do You Know?

38
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:33,141
The hottest place on Earth is the

39
00:01:33,241 --> 00:01:34,662
Lut Desert in Iran,

40
00:01:35,243 --> 00:01:37,826
where temperatures have been recorded as high

41
00:01:38,026 --> 00:01:44,092
as 159.3°F (70.7°C)!

42
00:01:44,753 --> 00:01:46,635
Imagine how hot it must be to

43
00:01:46,715 --> 00:01:47,836
have that much heat!

44
00:01:49,376 --> 00:01:49,943
Climate.

45
00:01:51,943 --> 00:01:54,527
Climate is the average weather condition of

46
00:01:54,647 --> 00:01:56,449
a place over a long period,

47
00:01:57,149 --> 00:01:58,811
usually 30 years or more.

48
00:01:59,811 --> 00:02:01,453
It tells us whether a place is

49
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:03,334
generally hot, cold,

50
00:02:03,935 --> 00:02:05,036
wet, or dry.

51
00:02:05,996 --> 00:02:08,518
For example, the climate of the Sahara

52
00:02:08,618 --> 00:02:10,280
Desert is hot and dry,

53
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:13,082
while the climate of the Amazon Rainforest

54
00:02:13,422 --> 00:02:14,683
is warm and rainy.

55
00:02:16,263 --> 00:02:17,993
Factors Affecting Climate.

56
00:02:19,993 --> 00:02:22,710
Several factors influence the climate of a

57
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:23,170
place.

58
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:26,057
Let us explore them one by one.

59
00:02:27,656 --> 00:02:30,491
Distance from the Equator (Latitudes).

60
00:02:32,491 --> 00:02:35,471
The Earth is divided into imaginary lines

61
00:02:35,731 --> 00:02:36,872
called latitudes.

62
00:02:37,873 --> 00:02:41,255
Places near the equator receive direct sunlight

63
00:02:41,395 --> 00:02:42,216
throughout the year,

64
00:02:42,836 --> 00:02:43,717
making them hot.

65
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:46,479
As we move towards the poles,

66
00:02:47,099 --> 00:02:48,320
sunlight spreads out,

67
00:02:48,901 --> 00:02:50,442
making these areas cooler.

68
00:02:51,382 --> 00:02:53,644
This is why tropical regions are warm,

69
00:02:54,244 --> 00:02:56,026
while polar regions are cold.

70
00:02:57,627 --> 00:02:58,270
Altitude.

71
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:02,416
Altitude is the height of a place

72
00:03:02,656 --> 00:03:03,557
above sea level.

73
00:03:04,478 --> 00:03:07,782
Higher altitudes have cooler temperatures because the

74
00:03:07,962 --> 00:03:10,205
air is thinner and cannot hold much

75
00:03:10,305 --> 00:03:10,705
heat.

76
00:03:11,446 --> 00:03:14,689
For example, mountains are colder than plains

77
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:16,151
at the same latitude.

78
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:20,692
Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and

79
00:03:20,772 --> 00:03:21,554
Land Breeze).

80
00:03:23,554 --> 00:03:26,301
Oceans and seas influence the climate of

81
00:03:26,441 --> 00:03:27,282
coastal areas.

82
00:03:28,322 --> 00:03:30,704
Water heats up and cools down more

83
00:03:30,784 --> 00:03:31,824
slowly than land.

84
00:03:32,705 --> 00:03:33,405
During the day,

85
00:03:34,026 --> 00:03:35,967
land heats up faster than water,

86
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,328
causing a sea breeze to blow from

87
00:03:38,408 --> 00:03:39,549
the sea to the land.

88
00:03:40,449 --> 00:03:43,031
At night, the land cools down quickly,

89
00:03:43,571 --> 00:03:45,512
and a land breeze blows from land

90
00:03:45,812 --> 00:03:46,293
to the sea.

91
00:03:47,073 --> 00:03:49,615
This keeps coastal areas cooler in summer

92
00:03:50,015 --> 00:03:52,616
and warmer in winter compared to inland

93
00:03:52,696 --> 00:03:53,157
regions.

94
00:03:54,717 --> 00:03:56,071
Direction of the Wind.

95
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,864
Winds carry heat and moisture from one

96
00:04:00,944 --> 00:04:01,905
place to another.

97
00:04:02,686 --> 00:04:04,868
Winds coming from the sea bring rain,

98
00:04:05,609 --> 00:04:08,152
while winds from deserts bring dry weather.

99
00:04:08,892 --> 00:04:12,036
For example, the monsoon winds bring heavy

100
00:04:12,136 --> 00:04:13,257
rainfall to India.

101
00:04:14,817 --> 00:04:15,512
Humidity.

102
00:04:17,512 --> 00:04:20,150
Humidity is the amount of water vapour

103
00:04:20,311 --> 00:04:20,851
in the air.

104
00:04:21,852 --> 00:04:25,256
Places with high humidity receive more rainfall,

105
00:04:25,897 --> 00:04:28,259
while dry areas have less humidity.

106
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:32,604
For example, coastal areas have higher humidity

107
00:04:32,904 --> 00:04:33,645
than deserts.

108
00:04:35,266 --> 00:04:36,230
Ocean Currents.

109
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:41,020
Ocean currents are large movements of water

110
00:04:41,261 --> 00:04:42,001
in the oceans.

111
00:04:43,042 --> 00:04:46,205
Warm ocean currents make coastal areas warmer,

112
00:04:46,766 --> 00:04:49,348
while cold currents bring cool temperatures.

113
00:04:50,229 --> 00:04:53,192
For example, the Gulf Stream warms Europe,

114
00:04:53,712 --> 00:04:56,595
while the cold Labrador Current cools Canada.

115
00:04:58,195 --> 00:04:59,305
Let's Learn More!

116
00:05:01,305 --> 00:05:04,601
Rainforests receive about 80 inches of rain

117
00:05:04,881 --> 00:05:07,384
each year and they are so important

118
00:05:07,845 --> 00:05:10,208
because they provide oxygen and food to

119
00:05:10,288 --> 00:05:10,688
the world.

120
00:05:11,429 --> 00:05:13,973
Without them, our planet would be very

121
00:05:14,053 --> 00:05:14,473
different!

122
00:05:16,012 --> 00:05:17,189
Types of Climate.

123
00:05:19,189 --> 00:05:21,507
Different parts of the world have different

124
00:05:21,587 --> 00:05:22,490
types of climate.

125
00:05:23,272 --> 00:05:24,815
Let's look at some major types.

126
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,591
Monsoon or Tropical Climate.

127
00:05:30,591 --> 00:05:31,904
Found in South Asia,

128
00:05:32,485 --> 00:05:35,249
Southeast Asia, and some parts of Africa.

129
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,734
It has hot summers and receives heavy

130
00:05:38,834 --> 00:05:40,897
rainfall during the monsoon season.

131
00:05:42,477 --> 00:05:43,798
Equatorial Climate.

132
00:05:45,798 --> 00:05:47,269
Found near the equator,

133
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:50,194
such as in the Amazon Rainforest and

134
00:05:50,294 --> 00:05:51,075
Congo Basin.

135
00:05:52,017 --> 00:05:54,080
It is hot and humid throughout the

136
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,842
year with heavy rainfall.

137
00:05:57,422 --> 00:05:58,441
Desert Climate.

138
00:06:00,441 --> 00:06:02,815
Found in places like the Sahara Desert

139
00:06:03,075 --> 00:06:04,077
and the Thar Desert.

140
00:06:04,978 --> 00:06:06,561
It has very little rainfall,

141
00:06:07,042 --> 00:06:09,026
hot days, and cold nights.

142
00:06:10,586 --> 00:06:11,612
Tundra Climate.

143
00:06:13,612 --> 00:06:14,888
Found near the poles,

144
00:06:15,409 --> 00:06:17,673
such as in Greenland and Antarctica.

145
00:06:18,555 --> 00:06:21,180
It is extremely cold with little or

146
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:22,202
no vegetation.

147
00:06:23,782 --> 00:06:24,430
Do You Know?

148
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:28,344
Antarctica is the driest,

149
00:06:28,765 --> 00:06:31,768
coldest, and windiest continent on Earth.

150
00:06:32,670 --> 00:06:34,792
It hasn’t rained there in millions of

151
00:06:34,872 --> 00:06:38,056
years, but it’s still considered a desert

152
00:06:38,377 --> 00:06:40,219
because of the lack of precipitation.

153
00:06:41,779 --> 00:06:43,733
Climatic Zones of the Earth.

154
00:06:45,733 --> 00:06:48,022
The Earth is divided into three main

155
00:06:48,123 --> 00:06:50,508
climatic zones based on latitude.

156
00:06:52,048 --> 00:06:52,906
Torrid Zone.

157
00:06:54,906 --> 00:06:57,611
Located between the Tropic of Cancer and

158
00:06:57,691 --> 00:06:58,913
the Tropic of Capricorn.

159
00:06:59,735 --> 00:07:01,678
It is the hottest zone as it

160
00:07:01,758 --> 00:07:03,281
receives direct sunlight.

161
00:07:04,821 --> 00:07:05,760
Temperate Zone.

162
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,074
Found between the tropics and the polar

163
00:07:10,155 --> 00:07:10,596
circles.

164
00:07:11,457 --> 00:07:14,544
It has moderate temperatures with distinct seasons.

165
00:07:16,084 --> 00:07:16,636
Do you know?

166
00:07:18,636 --> 00:07:20,627
There are different types of clouds that

167
00:07:20,707 --> 00:07:21,948
can tell you about the weather?

168
00:07:22,629 --> 00:07:25,934
For example, cumulus clouds are fluffy and

169
00:07:26,034 --> 00:07:26,956
show fair weather,

170
00:07:27,436 --> 00:07:30,441
while nimbostratus clouds bring rain or snow.

171
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:32,908
Frigid Zone.

172
00:07:34,908 --> 00:07:36,399
Located near the poles.

173
00:07:37,221 --> 00:07:39,848
It is the coldest zone with ice-covered

174
00:07:39,928 --> 00:07:40,310
lands.

175
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:42,561
Recall.

176
00:07:44,561 --> 00:07:47,490
Weather and climate are essential aspects of

177
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:48,331
our environment.

178
00:07:49,432 --> 00:07:51,754
Many factors, such as latitude,

179
00:07:52,234 --> 00:07:55,076
altitude, wind, and ocean currents,

180
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:56,478
influence climate.

181
00:07:57,579 --> 00:08:00,661
Different regions experience different types of climates,

182
00:08:01,242 --> 00:08:02,703
affecting the way people live,

183
00:08:03,264 --> 00:08:05,245
the food they grow and the clothes

184
00:08:05,345 --> 00:08:05,745
they wear.

185
00:08:07,286 --> 00:08:08,218
Let's Remember.

186
00:08:10,218 --> 00:08:13,111
Weather is the daily atmospheric condition of

187
00:08:13,211 --> 00:08:13,612
a place.

188
00:08:14,512 --> 00:08:16,914
Climate is the average weather over a

189
00:08:17,034 --> 00:08:17,754
long period.

190
00:08:18,615 --> 00:08:21,877
Latitude, altitude, distance from the sea,

191
00:08:22,378 --> 00:08:24,399
and winds influence climate.

192
00:08:25,159 --> 00:08:27,281
The world has different types of climate,

193
00:08:27,721 --> 00:08:30,023
including tropical, desert,

194
00:08:30,383 --> 00:08:30,943
and tundra.

195
00:08:31,724 --> 00:08:33,805
The Earth has three climatic zones:

196
00:08:34,406 --> 00:08:36,787
torrid, temperate, and frigid.

197
00:08:38,327 --> 00:08:39,098
Word Bank.

198
00:08:41,098 --> 00:08:41,498
Word.

199
00:08:42,336 --> 00:08:42,736
Meaning.

200
00:08:43,597 --> 00:08:44,197
Humidity.

201
00:08:44,998 --> 00:08:46,979
The amount of water vapor in the

202
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:47,580
air.

203
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:48,861
Altitude.

204
00:08:49,461 --> 00:08:51,363
The height of a place above sea

205
00:08:51,443 --> 00:08:51,823
level.

206
00:08:52,664 --> 00:08:53,204
Equator.

207
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:56,807
An imaginary line dividing the Earth into

208
00:08:56,927 --> 00:08:57,607
two halves.

209
00:08:58,588 --> 00:08:59,128
Monsoon.

210
00:08:59,849 --> 00:09:02,211
Seasonal winds that bring heavy rain.

211
00:09:03,151 --> 00:09:03,572
Tundra.

212
00:09:04,172 --> 00:09:06,734
A cold region with little vegetation.
